    "growth_divergence_warning": "Equity CAGR (11.6-12.3%) is less than half of EPS CAGR (25-29%): $2.1B of buybacks over FY2024-26 shrink book value and inflate per-share growth. Revenue CAGRs (15-17%) describe HOKA's hypergrowth phase, which has decelerated to high-single digits (Q1 FY2027 +8%). None of the historical CAGRs is a forward rate; guidance is used instead.",
    "notes": "FCF CAGRs use the owner-FCF series (reported FCF - SBC - equity-award withholding - interest income): FY2021 531.3, FY2023 397.2, FY2026 980.5. The 3-year figure is flattered by FY2023's inventory-build trough. Owner-FCF 5yr CAGR (13.0%) trails reported (14.2%) mostly because interest income on the cash pile grew from $2.6M to $63.6M, not because of SBC, which is modest (~0.8% of revenue). EPS series restated for the 6:1 split of Sep-2024 (FY2021 13.64 -> 2.27)."
  },
  "scenario_narratives": {
    "base": "Guidance year delivered, then HOKA settles at mid-single-digit growth as door expansion and Asia offset On/Nike/Adidas competition, and UGG's year-round diversification holds the brand without a fad collapse. Structural tariffs keep margins ~1pp under FY2027 guidance (22.5% EBITDA ex-SBC). The axes are HOKA's share trajectory in performance running and whether UGG's current cycle is a cycle or a platform.",
    "bull": "HOKA re-accelerates on sporting-goods distribution and international, UGG becomes a year-round lifestyle franchise, and tariff refunds plus DTC mix restore FY2025-26 margins (~25.5%). Revenue compounds ~8% for five years.",
    "bear": "UGG's fashion cycle rolls over and HOKA's deceleration turns into share loss: revenue falls ~9% over two years, wholesale destocks, promotions and tariffs take EBITDA ex-SBC to ~19% (FY2022-23 level). Two-brand concentration means there is no third leg to cushion it."
  },
  "valuation_philosophy": {
    "summary": "Owner-FCF DCF on a guidance-anchored FY2027 with margins drifting slightly below guidance on structural tariffs. At the anchor price DECK trades near 10.5x FY2027 guided EPS, below its 52-week range midpoint -- the market is pricing something between our base and bear cases, i.e. a UGG/HOKA fade. The valuation turns on brand durability, not on cost of capital or SBC (SBC is <1% of revenue, so house and street bases sit close together).",
    "key_risks_to_valuation": [
      "UGG fashion-cycle reversal (FY2012-16 precedent) -- half of revenue",
      "HOKA share loss to On, Nike and Adidas in specialty running",
      "Tariffs on Vietnam/Indonesia sourcing above the 12.5% guided rate; refunds uncertain",
      "Consumer discretionary slowdown hitting wholesale sell-in",
      "Terminal multiple: a 2-point swing in the cap moves base IV by roughly 8%"
    ]
  },
