    "notes": "MODEL: owner-FCF DCF, component build, 10-year horizon (routing: consumer-brand operating company, moderately cyclical; dcf-methods SKILL.md row 1/2). First valuation of DECK -- no prior DCF, no MEMORY entry. Owner FCF FY2026 = reported FCF 1,097.3 (OCF 1,182.0 - capex 84.6) - SBC incl. withholding 53.2 - interest income 63.6 = 980.5. Interest income stripped because net cash (1.60B) > 1x the FCF base. FY2026 cash tax paid was only 17.7% of pretax (234.3M), versus 27.6% in FY2025 and a 22.8% book ETR -- timing, not structure, so the path runs at 23%. Year-1 EBITDA margin anchored to FY2027 guidance (revenue $5.86-5.91B, EPS $7.35-7.50, gross margin ~56.5% vs 57.7% on a 12.5% effective tariff rate, no refunds assumed): implied operating margin ~21.2%, EBITDA ex-SBC ~23.4% vs 25.3% in FY2026. Working capital is a genuine drag for a wholesale/DTC footwear distributor (AR 319 + inventory 487 - AP 385 = 421M at FYE, ~7.7% of revenue), so wc_capture is -8%. Buybacks: a heavy repurchaser ($1,075M FY2026, $338M Q1 FY2027, $4.7B authorization left) -- the flat count is well funded; buybacks below IV are accretive and are NOT credited in the model. Possible tariff refunds (~$120M paid) are not modelled. Quarterly CSV labels run one fiscal year behind (CSV 'Q2 2026' = Q1 FY2027, quarter to 2026-06-30).",
